# Raven-Targeter

A cross-platform desktop application that discovers **recently created or
recently active, user-created AI API projects on GitHub** — unofficial
wrappers, SDKs, proxies, gateways, OpenAI-compatible adapters, and related
issues/PRs — for a configurable set of AI provider targets.

Default targets: OpenAI, Anthropic (Claude), Google Gemini, xAI (Grok),
DeepSeek.

Every result comes from a real GitHub API response and keeps its source URL,
evidence, and timestamps. This tool does not ask an LLM what it remembers —
it searches real public GitHub data.

## V1 Scope

- GitHub repository search
- GitHub code search (used for implementation evidence within shortlisted
  repos — GitHub's code search API doesn't support date filters, so repos
  are shortlisted by repo/issue search first)
- GitHub issue search
- README enrichment for shortlisted repositories
- 10-day (configurable) UTC-based date validation, distinguishing
  `created_at` / `updated_at` / `pushed_at`
- Deterministic (non-LLM) classification and relevance/freshness scoring
- Deduplication by canonical URL and repository identity
- SQLite persistence
- Desktop GUI: Dashboard, Search, Results, Settings
- JSON/CSV export

**Not in V1** (see `AGENTS.md` for the full list and rationale): general web
search, Reddit/HN/package-registry adapters, public shared-chat-page
discovery, LLM summarization, headless browsers, or executing any code from
discovered repositories.

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # or .venv\Scripts\activate on Windows
pip install -e ".[dev]"
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env and add your GITHUB_TOKEN (recommended — see below)
```

## Environment Variables

| Variable                        | Default                        | Description                                  |
| -------------------------------- | ------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |
| `GITHUB_TOKEN`                   | *(none)*                        | GitHub personal access token. Strongly recommended — see below. |
| `RAVEN_TARGETS`                  | `openai,anthropic,gemini,grok,deepseek` | Comma-separated target providers. |
| `RAVEN_LOOKBACK_DAYS`            | `10`                             | How many days back to search. |
| `RAVEN_MAX_RESULTS_PER_SOURCE`   | `200`                            | Max accepted results per source per run. |
| `RAVEN_DB_URL`                   | `sqlite:///data/raven.db`        | SQLAlchemy database URL. |
| `RAVEN_LOG_LEVEL`                | `INFO`                           | `DEBUG` / `INFO` / `WARNING` / `ERROR`. |

### About `GITHUB_TOKEN`

The app runs without one, but **unauthenticated GitHub API requests are
limited to 60/hour**, which is not enough for real search runs. With a token,
the limit is 5,000/hour. Create a fine-grained personal access token with
read-only public repository access at
https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens and put it in `.env`.
**Never commit `.env` or the token value anywhere.**

## Running the GUI

```bash
python app.py
```

## Running Tests

```bash
pytest
ruff check .
```

## Limitations

- V1 only searches GitHub. No general web search, no Reddit/HN, no public
  shared-chat-page discovery yet.
- Gist discovery is a documented, disabled-by-default placeholder — GitHub
  has no full-text Gist search API.
- Classification and scoring are deterministic rule-based systems, not LLM
  judgment — they can be wrong or conservative (results fall back to
  `unknown` classification when evidence is weak, by design).
- This is a discovery/analysis tool only. It never clones or executes code
  from discovered repositories.

## Planned (Future) Web-Search Layer

A later version may add a web-search adapter layer (general search engines,
Reddit, Hacker News, package registries) as described in the original
product manifest. That work is intentionally deferred and requires its own
scoping pass — particularly for anything touching public shared-chat pages
from other AI platforms, which raises separate scope/ToS questions beyond
what V1 covers.
